      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks for this—it's a really solid foundation. I like the balance you've struck.\n\nOne thing though, I'm a little unsure about the \"persistent itch\" metaphor. It's a bit... I don't know, physical? It feels a little off for a formal performance document. \n\nCould we try to find a different way to describe that \"nagging nuisance\" aspect? I'm looking for something that captures how the lateness feels like this small, uninvited, almost mischievous element that creeps in and messes with our perfectly planned morning. It's not a huge, obvious blow, but it's this little, disruptive presence that we just can't quite pin down or get rid of. \n\nCan you try to rewrite that \"Areas for Improvement\" section using a metaphor that feels a bit more... alive? Something that captures that sense of a small, irritating, and somewhat unpredictable force that disrupts our flow? We can keep the rest of the review as is.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
